0 -28 Td
(Goal: run Hermes as a Discord bot that can join a voice channel and use OpenAI Realtime speech-to-speech.) Tj
0 -20 Td
(Architecture:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Discord RTP/Opus -> PCM -> OpenAI Realtime WebSocket -> Discord voice playback.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(For long work, Realtime calls a safe Hermes subagent handoff tool and posts durable output to the text channel.) Tj
0 -28 Td
(Prerequisites:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(1. Discord application and bot token from https://discord.com/developers/applications.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. OpenAI Platform API key from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys with Realtime access.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. Hermes Agent installed from package or source checkout.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. ffmpeg, Opus, Python voice dependencies, and a running Hermes gateway.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(5. Bot permissions: View Channels, Send Messages, Read History, Connect, Speak, Use Voice Activity.) Tj
0 -28 Td
(Install basics:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(macOS: brew install ffmpeg opus portaudio espeak-ng) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Ubuntu/Debian: sudo apt install ffmpeg libopus0 portaudio19-dev espeak-ng) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Python: python -m pip install -U "hermes-agent[messaging,voice]" "discord.py[voice]" "PyNaCl>=1.5.0" davey websockets) Tj
ET
